	(text "60 V in, 1.5 A. The 36 V LMR33630 was rejected because it sits UNDER the clamp (D-273)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 104.1400 60.9600 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.20 1.20)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "821b80f9-1541-4c87-b60b-ba81e88ae7f1")
	)
	(text "~0.8 A peak on +5 V: the Teensy, the transceiver, the IMU,\nthe three sender excitations and the radio (D-273)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 106.6800 53.3400 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.20 1.20)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "62ff1ff6-cd64-45fa-a47b-d5b2d97ed82a")
	)
	(text "IC15 - a single pour, star-tied at this pin" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1000 149.8600 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.20 1.20)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "6230c5a4-5c2f-4e50-9562-15d1adf89b74")
	)
	(text "F1 is 4 A because the 900-1000 nit bar and its scaler draw about 2.5 A at 12 V (D-269, D-273)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 81.2800 95.2500 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.20 1.20)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "6ce583aa-db32-47b4-97d7-64d1e4b84dc3")
	)
	(text "P-channel high side, >= 60 V for the same reason as the buck." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 127.0000 97.7900 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.20 1.20)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "bb0fd105-dcdd-497a-bf6b-b55339b8e6ca")
	)
	(text "D-273 offers two ways to switch the backlight: Q1 with its own\ndrive, or U2 in place of all five parts. Fit one. Never both." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 213.3600 137.1600 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.20 1.20)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "c6081e08-0a66-4447-a65f-cd970cbe18ea")
	)
	(text "+3V3 is the Teensy's own 3.3 V output, arriving at the socket. There is NO 3.3 V\nregulator on this carrier: D-273 put the radio on the XIAO module's own LDO because a\nBLE scan peaks near 300 mA and the Teensy's regulator is a 250 mA part. TARGET.md\nsection 1 still says 'LDO for the ESP32-C3' - the CSV wins and this sheet follows it." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 190.5000 152.4000 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.30 1.30)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "6ee42b59-f5bc-4152-b51c-ee48e8385fa1")
	)
	(text "the flag says where +3V3 is driven from - the socket, not a regulator" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 218.4400 180.3400 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.10 1.10)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "d61eac72-570c-40f2-8ea6-c3c645926824")
	)
	(text "BUS - CAN2" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 396.2400 13.9700 0)
		(effects (font (size 3.20 3.20)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "8bf3c688-5b0a-45d9-8d39-7c32aed869a8")
	)
	(text "500 kbps. NO termination on this board: D-079's far-end 120 ohm moved to the dash\nnode when the engine-bay drop was released (D-318 -> D-346). The common-mode choke\nis a DNP footprint for that same reason - the field says so, not a comment." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 396.2400 20.3200 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.40 1.40)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "22dbb2e4-1784-476c-bf91-ef76b3d3c71f")
	)
	(text "IC16. Out: 0x200, 0x210, 0x218, and the battery frames 0x220 / 0x221 (D-345).\nIn: 0x180 extended, 29-bit big-endian, from the AEM wideband (D-266)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 398.7800 99.0600 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.20 1.20)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "c941fba7-5d8a-44de-8237-6179595af3d3")
	)
	(text "ANALOG IN - one stage, drawn nine times" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 10.1600 204.4700 0)
		(effects (font (size 3.20 3.20)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "284bd7fc-cfb8-4d90-9ef6-79c825889846")
	)
	(text "Every channel ends in the same three parts and every one is drawn: series or divider resistor, 100 nF, BAT54S to +3V3 and GND.\nNone of them is abbreviated or hidden behind a symbol, because the whole point of drawing this is that a missing clamp is visible." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 10.1600 210.8200 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.50 1.50)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "84d64f39-21bd-4699-86b9-e94d9ca1b978")
	)
