	)
	(text "BAT54S is a SERIES pair, A - COM - K, and the direction is the whole point: COM carries the signal, A goes to GROUND so a negative\nexcursion is caught by GND - COM, and K goes to +3V3 so a positive one is caught by COM - +3V3. Drawn the other way round it clamps\nnothing and puts a diode path from +3V3 to ground through the sender. The first pass of this sheet had it backwards; the drawing is\nwhat found it, which is the argument for drawing it (README, 'Why a schematic at all')." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 76.2000 350.5200 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.30 1.30)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "266a4b33-35c4-49bc-abe6-36f3cb7c2cf4")
	)
	(text "The jumpers are why this board outlives the 12A (D-262): open J1 or J3 and the same x0.4 divider reads a 0-5 V transducer instead of a\nresistive sender. J7 is a footprint only - there is no oil-temperature sender on the 12A and no conductor run for one (D-264), so\nDP-ICU-B 7 carries a sealing plug and the swap's rebuilt leg lands there." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 76.2000 360.6800 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.30 1.30)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "eb2b452e-e18e-463f-8ef0-50e4ff0cf072")
	)
	(text "PULSE IN - the two that are not copies of anything" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 10.1600 382.2700 0)
		(effects (font (size 3.20 3.20)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "ed9b2869-128e-44e6-8455-e9f9b5c5d591")
	)
