		(uuid "b4272f58-2cd4-4ca0-8bc5-1c24f51b3bb9")
	)
	(text "Trailing coil negative primary: hundreds of volts of inductive kick (luxury D-304). 2 pulses per revolution.\nThe comparator sits on +5 V DELIBERATELY. Its common-mode input range stops about 1.5 V under its supply,\nso on 3.3 V the 5.1 V zener node would clip and the tach would read nothing above idle. That is the fact\nwhich is invisible in prose and obvious in a drawing, and it is the whole argument for drawing this." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7000 394.9700 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.25 1.25)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "2a8ce12f-316d-438e-a926-29b14be226ce")
	)
	(text "the open-collector output is pulled up to +3V3, NOT to +5 V - that is what\nlets a comparator running on 5 V drive a 3.3 V-only input safely" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 167.6400 411.4800 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "46be09f7-ae02-43da-8f66-f7050d8a39bf")
	)
	(text "The reference and the feedback are DERIVED ON THIS SHEET and are not in the record: 5 x 12/51 = 1.18 V at the reference,\nand 1.2 M against the 200 k source gives 3.3 x 200/1400 = 0.47 V of hysteresis, which is the 'about 0.5 V' the record asks for.\nThey are a proposal, not a fact. Whether an LM393 or an H11L1 opto goes here is a BENCH RESULT (icu_channels IC04) and\nnothing drawn here settles whether this stage survives a trailing coil at 6000 rpm. If it picks up noise, the opto replaces it all." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7000 462.2800 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.25 1.25)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "adb4b73b-8116-4738-9a19-01553bc259fa")
	)
	(text "IC08  road speed - DP-ICU-B 8" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 304.8000 389.8900 0)
		(effects (font (size 2.00 2.00)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "948bdd58-ffd3-4767-a21e-34cacfbd1ee0")
	)
	(text "A 12 V square wave from the Hall pulse generator on the transmission's\nspeedo-drive boss (D-272). One jumper picks the front end. Fit ONE." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 304.8000 394.9700 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.25 1.25)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "b55d57b4-8f95-4827-9448-977d4ad370be")
	)
	(text "J8A pulls the node to +3V3 for an open-collector sensor. J8B makes a 10 k / 4.7 k divider\nfor a push-pull output, which lands at 12 x 4.7/14.7 = 3.84 V - above the rail, which is\nexactly why the BAT54S is there and is not optional. Pulses per mile is a config value,\ntrued once against a measured mile (D-272)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 304.8000 452.1200 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.25 1.25)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "da227a85-aaf3-47f4-b0e9-11948002867a")
	)
	(text "DISPLAY AND LOCAL" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 548.6400 382.2700 0)
		(effects (font (size 3.20 3.20)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "05fa4e5e-ea8e-49e2-8782-84e3187fb485")
	)
	(text "IC21 ribbons to the BT817 board, then a TFP410-class encoder and the 1920 x 720 bar's scaler,\nall of it off this board (chain ii, D-269). The backlight's 12 V comes from J2 and never from\nthis header. V-084 confirms the pixel clock and sync polarity against the real panel; nothing\non this sheet does, and drawing it neatly does not close it." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 548.6400 388.6200 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.25 1.25)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "9da56f81-88ce-4c71-936d-635aa6259688")
	)
	(text "IC22  page button - momentary, by the display" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 701.0400 403.8600 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.50 1.50)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "17e8ad88-9abf-4e51-95f1-835197474e47")
	)
	(text "IC23 - the I2C pull-ups live here because the bus is board-local" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 551.1800 533.4000 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.20 1.20)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "44445cc9-2f5a-498d-bb32-341cb7195b51")
	)
	(text "The antenna end overhangs the board edge with a 5 mm keep-out toward an RF-transparent\nenclosure wall (D-265's edge rule becomes D-270's face rule). Scan the advertisement\nalways; open FFE1 only when cell detail is wanted; never write. FEE7 and any DFU\ncharacteristic are never touched - that is the door to a bricked pack (D-330, D-345)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 762.0000 485.1400 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.20 1.20)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "446a2a29-234e-4491-9714-94f847a0df87")
	)
	(text "THE PROCESSOR BOUNDARY" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 1018.5400 128.2700 0)
		(effects (font (size 2.60 2.60)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "3e1b0c4c-2d20-4fff-82f6-1e4f6073b89b")
	)
	(text "The Teensy is drawn as the SOCKET it plugs into and nothing more.\n\nThe reason is R11 and CONVENTIONS section 2.8: the record assigns no\nTeensy pin numbers anywhere. icu_channels says 'ADC', 'digital, input\ncapture', 'QSPI header', 'I2C', 'Serial2 + 2 GPIO' - and stops. Drawing\na pinout would put facts on this sheet that the record does not have,\nand a schematic that quietly picks an answer is worse than one with a\nquestion mark on it. The pin numbers below are ordinal: they say which\nnets reach the socket, not where.\n\nThe 8 MB PSRAM (APS6404L-3SQR) is not on this sheet either - it solders\nto the Teensy's own underside pads, not to the carrier.\n\nPin assignment happens with the layout (F2) and the firmware. When it\ndoes it becomes a row in the record first, and a wire here second." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 1018.5400 137.1600 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.30 1.30)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "93b7e7c2-1a81-4e31-bb4c-40c67506a08a")
	)
	(text "WHAT THIS SHEET DOES NOT KNOW" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 612.1400 13.9700 0)
		(effects (font (size 2.60 2.60)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "2fc5794d-398e-4e15-90bd-bf07f8231914")
	)
	(text "ERC-clean means this drawing is consistent with itself. It does not mean the board works, and the two are different claims.\nEverything below is unmeasured. Drawing it neatly closes none of it:\n\n   V-084    the BT817's pixel clock and sync polarity against the actual panel. Not measured.\n   Q-308    the oil-temperature sender, and with it IC07's pull-up value. No part chosen, so that resistor carries a question\n            mark and not a number - a footprint with a '?' is honest, a plausible value would not be.\n   D-261    the IC01 and IC03 sender curves - three-point reads on the senders IN THE CAR, not from a datasheet.\n   IC04     LM393 against H11L1 is a bench result, not a preference. The hysteresis values here are derived on this sheet.\n   layout   every module and socket pin NUMBER. Functional pins are named; numbers are ordinal and are fixed at F2.\n\nScope. Schematic only, and there is no .kicad_pcb in this folder on purpose: fabricating a carrier has a lead time, a cost and a\nrevision cycle, which makes it BIG by CLAUDE.md section 3 and therefore a block before any time goes into a layout - not an\nassumption that follows from a schematic existing. The carrier can be protoboard for bring-up.\n\nThe harness is not here and never will be. Gauge, colour, bundles, cavities and cut lengths are the record's job and KiCad has no\nmodel for any of them. DP-ICU-A and DP-ICU-B appear on this sheet only as pins on the board edge; what is on the other side of\nthem belongs to cavities.csv, and if this sheet and a row ever disagree, the row is right." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 612.1400 21.5900 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.30 1.30)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "1c136d2f-1c71-40d9-b1a2-1b96adb4f854")
	)
